=== src/game/entities/player/README.md (modified, +1/-1) ===

CHANGES IN CONTEXT (file after this PR, 41 lines, windows around the changes; `+` added line, `-` removed line):
   ...
   22: 
   23: `src/tests/CheckManagerIsolation.cmake` puts every file in this tree, subdirectories included, on exactly one of two lists; a file on neither fails `ctest`.
   24: 
   25: - **`MANAGER_FILES`** are managers: a piece of the character's state and the rules over it, built and tested in `mangos_tests` without a character. A manager never names the character class: no include of `Player.h`, no pointer, reference, member or alias of the class, and not the word itself, comments included. It takes everything it needs (guid, name, game time, template lookups) as parameters. `src/tests/CheckHeaderReach.cmake` also keeps each manager's includes from reaching `Player.h`, `Unit.h`, the session or the object manager.
   26: - **`OWNER_FILES`** are the character's own side: `Player.h`, `Player.cpp`, every `Player*.cpp`, `PlayerRegistry`, `PlayerTaxi`, `PlayerPetCache` and this README, plus the older managers that still name the class until each one is converted.
   27: 
